ne] The two had a nephew, Sir Gawain, who was named after King Arthur's favored Titan, Gawain. [Huntik.com]\n\nKing Arthur's island, Avalon, became the resting place of the one of the most powerful Casterwill family artifacts, the Willblade. [Knight of the Willblade]"},{"heading":"Abilities","level":2,"wikitext":"","text":""},{"heading":"Bonded Titans","level":3,"wikitext":"*[[Gawain]]\n\n[[Category:Characters]]\n[[Category:Seekers]]\n[[Category:Historical figures]]\n[[Category:Deceased characters]]\n[[Category:Knights of the Round Table]]","text":"*Gawain"}],"full_text":"King Arthur of Camelot was the head of the Knights of the Round Table and the husband of Guinevere. The legends of King Arthur are a central part of English and Medieval folklore, and include stories of Arthur's island of Avalon, resting place of the Willblade. His symbol was famously a dragon. \n\n== History ==\nKing Arthur was married to Guinevere. His champion, Sir Lancelot, fell from grace by falling in love with Guinevere. [Memory Lane] The two had a nephew, Sir Gawain, who was named after King Arthur's favored Titan, Gawain. [Huntik.com]\n\nKing Arthur's island, Avalon, became the resting place of the one of the most powerful Casterwill family artifacts, the Willblade. [Knight of the Willblade]\n\n== Abilities ==\n=== Bonded Titans ===\n*Gawain","raw_wikitext":"{{infobox character\n| image     = File:Placeholder person.png\n| wife      = [[Guinevere]]\n| relations = Sir Gawain (nephew) \n| base      = Camelot\n| group     = [[Knights of the Round Table]]\n| first     = \"[[Memory Lane]]\" (mentioned)\n| last      = \n| gender    = Male\n| hair      = \n| eyes      =\n}}\n'''King Arthur''' of Camelot was the head of the [[Knights of the Round Table]] and the husband of [[Guinevere]]. The legends of King Arthur are a central part of English and Medieval folklore, and include stories of Arthur's island of [[Avalon]], resting place of the [[Willblade]]. His symbol was famously a dragon. \n\n== History ==\nKing Arthur was married to Guinevere. His champion, [[Sir Lancelot]], fell from grace by falling in love with Guinevere. {{source|Memory Lane}} The two had a nephew, [[Sir Gawain]], who was named after King Arthur's favored Titan, [[Gawain]]. {{source|Huntik.com}}\n\nKing Arthur's island, [[Avalon]], became the resting place of the one of the most powerful [[Casterwill family]] artifacts, the [[Willblade]]. {{Source|Knight of the Willblade}}\n\n== Abilities ==\n=== Bonded Titans ===\n*[[Gawain]]\n\n[[Category:Characters]]\n[[Category:Seekers]]\n[[Category:Historical figures]]\n[[Category:Deceased characters]]\n[[Category:Knights of the Round Table]]","categories":["Characters","Deceased characters","Historical figures","Knights of the Round Table","Seekers"],"links":[{"target_title":"Guinevere","label":"Guinevere","target_id":"huntik:page:26961","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Guinevere","status":"resolved","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A26961"},{"target_title":"Knights of the Round Table","label":"Knights of the Round Table","target_id":"huntik:page:26962","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Knights_of_the_Round_Table","status":"resolved","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A26962"},{"target_title":"Memory Lane","label":"Memory Lane","target_id":"huntik:page:5037","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Memory_Lane","status":"resolved","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A5037"},{"target_title":"Knights of the Round Table","label":"Knights of the Round Table","target_id":"huntik:page:26962","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Knights_of_the_Round_Table","status":"resolved","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A26962"},{"target_title":"Guinevere","label":"Guinevere","target_id":"huntik:page:26961","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Guinevere","status":"resolved","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A26961"},{"target_title":"Avalon","label":"Avalon","target_id":"huntik:page:9191","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Avalon",